<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>report-outline-brief.md</title><style>body{font:18px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1rem;color:#17252d;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #777;padding:.5rem}a{color:#064b8c}</style><main><h1>Adapt the decision brief into three presentation pages — learner brief</h1>
<p>Fictional Northstar Services training material.</p>
<h2>Approved fictional facts</h2>
<p>F1 September budget USD 200,000.
F2 actual USD 218,000; supplied variance USD 18,000 / 9%.
F3 approved explanation USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel.
F4 forecast revision proposed, unapproved.
F5 operations lead must confirm remaining contractor end date by September 25.</p>
<h2>Supplied options</h2>
<p>D1 maintain support one month, estimated incremental USD 8,000.
D2 reduce support, estimated two-week delay.
D3 controller recommends D1; CFO decision requested September 26. Neither option approved.
D4 revenue effect unknown. Estimates are fictional writing inputs.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>The CFO will discuss the same decision in a short leadership meeting. Specify the message of each page.</p>
<h2>Actions</h2>
<ol>
<li>Assign one purpose to each page: situation, supplied options, decision.</li>
<li>Ask AI for three factual titles and brief speaker notes.</li>
<li>Check that titles do not imply revenue impact or approval that the packet does not establish.</li>
<li>Write a plain-text equivalent for the suggested comparison table.</li>
<li>Reconcile dates, amounts, and recommendation status across all pages.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Output</h2>
<p>Three page titles; key message per page; supporting facts; speaker notes; text equivalent of any suggested visual.</p>
</main></html>